Z||000008||NOS3800||10-09-2001||12:15 AM||||As fAR AS THE 300zx GOES, THIS IS THE LOT IN FRONT OF THE bODYsHOP WE WORK AT. nOT TO TOOT my own horn, But I put that car together. Did all the body work. It was rough. Didn't turn out quite like I wanted, it was the first body kit we have done, and learned a few things. One being that body kits fit like **** ! Spent hours getting it to look descent, not perfect. The rockers aren't attached yet in  the pic. I did those today. BTW, the car isn't a turbo, its a poser. Engine compartment is FILTHY, car has 150,000 miles on it too. The Escort is another ricer. It was an all over, that I did. L1LDVil painted both.<BR>TOOT TOOT<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sig_Pic,_nos3800_3.jpg"> <BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.21@102.13 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||1
Z||000009||lildevil||10-09-2001||07:46 PM||||You guys that bought that style spoiler i have a question. Does it come all the way down to the edge of the decklid on the back or does it stop halfway .  I ve seen many that stop halfway down...to the key hole.  Seen only one other like mine that go all the way to edge. That was on Keith Gerards IMSA conversion.  I know his and mine cam from IRM. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Raydar||10-09-2001||08:09 PM||||I have the same (IRM) spoiler on my 88 coupe. Comes all the way to the bottom of the lid. Also have another one from Race Tech/Fiero Shop (crappy quality, BTW). It comes to the middle of the lock cylinder.<BR>The one that RS Motorsports sells also stops at the lock.<P>lildevil, <BR>Was your spoiler warped when you got it? The bottom edge of mine doesn't quite touch the decklid on the sides, kind of above the cutouts in the rear fascia. Does that even make sense? The center meets the lid just fine. Also, if you look at the very top edge, the center is lower than the corners. Almost looks like it's supposed to be that way, but I don't think it is.<BR>THIS is the reason that I bought Race Tech's spoiler, but THAT one is so warped on the sides that I don't know if I can even bolt it down without breaking the deck lid.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> <BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 10-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||88CoupeV6||10-10-2001||10:40 AM||||I must be the only one that doesn't have a liking for that spoiler  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I love the stock Fiero one though<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig.jpg">    <BR>:D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||9
Z||000012||ChopTop||10-10-2001||11:49 AM||||I ordered mine from IRM.  It comes all the way down to the bottom of the original decklid and it is slightly wider than the stock decklid.  Also, there is a slight bow in the center.  I laid a straight edge to it and it's about 1/2 lower in the center.   I had it on my notchback for awhile, then tried it after I had the top chopped, that was a laugh, my rearview mail slot window turned into a mailslit, so much for that idea.  I think it looks best on the IMSA style Fiero's.  Not sure what I'm going to do with it, as of right now I do not want to sell it.||||reg||1
